✅ What is ExecutorService in Java?
ExecutorService is an interface in Java’s java.util.concurrent package that provides a higher-level replacement for managing threads manually.
Instead of creating and managing threads yourself (new Thread()), ExecutorService helps you efficiently manage thread pools and run tasks concurrently.

ExecutorService is used to manage threads and Using Callable with Future when your thread needs to return a result or throw an exception.


🔹 Why use ExecutorService?
Avoid manual thread creation and management.

Reuse a pool of threads → better performance.

Control over task execution (timeout, cancel, shutdown).

Scales better for large/multiple tasks.

